   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "SDXL Outpaint + Upscale (Image Recall)\n\n1. Drop a PNG onto the Image Recall node (on the node, NOT the empty canvas, which would load the PNG's own workflow). The box under it shows the checkpoint, LoRAs, prompts and settings it found.\n2. Outpaint Canvas: pick the aspect (16:9, 9:16, 21:9 ...) and where the original sits (center = grow both sides, left = grow to the right).\n3. prompt_prefix is put in front of the recalled prompt: describe the wider scene there (\"wide shot, desert stretching to the horizon\").\n4. Queue. Pass 1 fills the new area at SDXL size (~1MP), the original pixels are pasted back, RealESRGAN x4 upscales, the image is resized to the exact ratio (16:9 x2 = 2688x1512), and Tiled Refine re-details it in 1024px tiles.\n\nTuning\n- Tiled Refine denoise: 0.2 stays close to the upscale, 0.4 adds more detail (and more change). Seams: raise overlap to 192.\n- Seam between old and new area: raise feather on Outpaint Canvas.\n- New area ignores the scene: write more in prompt_prefix, or set prompt_override.\n- Missing checkpoint/LoRA: shown with ! in the info box; pick a checkpoint by hand."
   ],
   "title": "How to use",
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  }
 ],
